# DTF tier manifest: lifecycle-sweep-derived-state  (artifact-keeper#6469)
#
# THE BUG (#6469, found by the #6333 audit)
#   A lifecycle/retention sweep soft-deletes in bulk SQL
#   (LifecycleService::execute_in_repository), so it never reaches the
#   per-artifact delete's post-commit steps (ArtifactService::finish_delete
#   and the REST delete handler). After a sweep:
#     * Maven: the stored maven-metadata.xml `mvn deploy` uploaded still lists
#       the swept version in <versions>/<latest>/<release>, and the stored
#       SNAPSHOT version-level document still names the swept build;
#     * Cargo: the sparse-index file stays cached (300 s) and keeps listing
#       the swept version, in the repository and in a Virtual over it; the
#       REST delete had the same gap (the cache was cleared on publish only);
#     * peers: no delete sync task, so push/mirror peers keep the version;
#     * audit: no ARTIFACT_DELETED row;
#     * events: no artifact.deleted, so no webhook delivery;
#     * search: the OpenSearch document is never removed.
#
# THE ORACLE (oracle.sh)
#   Each case publishes two versions, backdates one with SQL, runs a
#   max_age_days policy on that repository through the execute API, and
#   reads the derived state:
#     Maven:   GET maven-metadata.xml (GA level and SNAPSHOT level);
#     Cargo:   GET the sparse index on the Local and the Virtual, warmed
#              before the sweep; and the same after a REST delete;
#     generic: SQL on sync_tasks, audit_log and webhook_deliveries, and the
#              mock OpenSearch request log (BULK delete lines).
#   CONTROLs (both images): each sweep removes exactly the aged rows; a REST
#   delete in the generic repository produces the delete task, the audit row,
#   the webhook delivery and the search DELETE, so the probes can see them.
#   FIX cases are RED on main and GREEN on the fix.
#
# PROFILES
#   search.mock-opensearch: OPENSEARCH_URL toward the logging mock;
#   webhooks.mock-receiver + webhooks.v2-producer: a webhook target and the
#   producer that writes webhook_deliveries. Filesystem storage.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~80 authenticated calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem search.mock-opensearch webhooks.mock-receiver webhooks.v2-producer"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
